WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:13.809
It’s likely that you’ve already heard
of

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:30.990
Coco

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.380
Chanel either from her famous perfume, or
the luxury clothing brand based on her name.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:41.270
As a woman trying to build a business in a
time where the world was controlled by men,

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.190
Chanel started at less-than-zero.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:48.370
And yet she found a way to climb to the position
of being one of the most wealthy and powerful

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.290
women in the world.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:55.970
On today’s Biographics, we are here to tell
you the true rags-to-riches story of Coco

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.260
Chanel.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:05.320
Early Life
Gabrielle Chanel was born on August 19th,

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.880
1883 in France’s Loire Valley.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.870
Her mother, Eugénie Jeanne Devolle, was an
unwed laundry woman.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.300
She gave birth to Gabrielle in a charity hospital
run by nuns.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.410
On the day she was born, her mother had to
write “traveling” where the father’s

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.410
name should be.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.170
That wasn’t just an excuse for an absentee
dad, though, because Albert Chanel traveled

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.950
from town to town selling clothing to local
peasants.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:30.220
Gabrielle had one older sister, Julia, and
they were less than a year apart.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.240
The couple had their hands full with two infant
daughters, and they could hardly scrape by

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.760
with what money they had.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.250
In 1884, Albert and Jeanne’s family gave
them money so that they could pay for a marriage

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.250
license.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.630
After their union was official, they had several
more children, and the family all lived in

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.280
a cramped one-room apartment in the town of
Brive-la-Gaillarde.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.050
Gabrielle learned how to sew at an early age
to help her father with his clothing business.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.190
But when she was just 12 years old, Gabrielle’s
mother became sick, and died.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.820
Raising young children is very much a full-time
job, so he could not earn an income and take

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.280
care of them at the same time.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.370
He sent his sons to work on a farm, and the
girls were sent to a convent called Aubazine

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:06.740
to be raised by nuns.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.959
The nuns taught her discipline, as well as
how to read and write.

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:14.670
She learned to carry herself with the grace
and elegance of a lady, rather than a peasant.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.120
Most of the other children living in the convent
were orphans.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.500
But since her father was still alive, Gabrielle
refused to consider herself an orphan, too.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.810
She held onto the hope that her father would
return one day, and that they could be a family

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:26.810
again.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.410
Books were a way for her to get lost in a
world of fantasy.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:35.990
She began to create elaborate stories about
her own life, as well, to help ease the pain

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:37.040
of her reality.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.780
Later in life, one of the most common stories
she told her friends was how she was raised

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.230
by her strict “Aunties”.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:47.690
She continued giving lies and half-truths
about her past, which made it almost impossible

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:53.060
for anyone to know just how difficult her
childhood truly had been.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:03:00.290
Becoming “Coco”
At age 18, Gabrielle left the convent to find

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.290
a job.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.290
There were very few opportunities for women
to find work, but she was lucky to have the

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.520
sewing skills she learned from her father.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.410
She worked as a seamstress during the day,
making clothing for rich ladies in the town

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:11.410
of Moulins.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:16.870
This was a very solitary job, and she was
hidden in a backroom working long hours mending

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:17.930
and assembling garments.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.470
At night, she worked a second job at a nightclub,
where she would sing and dance in front of

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.470
a crowd.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:27.260
When she was 23, her act caught the attention
of a man named Etienne Balsan.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.970
He was the wealthy heir to the Balsan garment
company, which supplied the French army with

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.970
its uniforms.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.870
Gabrielle Chanel started going by the nickname
“Coco”.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.819
Years later, even Chanel herself would tell
everyone a different story of where the name

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:39.819
came from.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.960
Some believe it was based on the lyrics of
a song she used to sing.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.710
Others think it’s short for the French word
“Cocotte”, which means “a kept woman”-

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.850
or- in today’s slang, “sugar baby”.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:53.319
For someone in Gabrielle Chanel’s situation,
these wealthy men were the only hope she had

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:55.069
of escaping poverty.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:58.650
Balsan had a “type”- which was aspiring
actresses.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:03.269
The girlfriend who lived with him before Chanel
was named Emilienne d’Alencon, and she went

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:06.430
on to become rich and famous with her successful
career in Paris.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.560
Gabrielle had no delusions about the relationship
with Etienne Balsan, and she knew that by

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.240
sleeping with him, he would help introduce
her to the right people.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:18.989
But after a few auditions, it was clear that
she just wasn’t cut out for show business.

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:23.229
She was staying at Balsan’s house in the
country, the Chateau de Royallieu for a few

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.229
days.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:28.300
The home was set in the middle of the forest,
where Balsan enjoyed riding horses and hunting.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.979
When his guests came over for the weekend,
he kept her like his dirty little secret,

00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:35.069
telling her to hide in one of the back bedrooms.

00:04:35.069 --> 00:04:37.169
This was infuriating for Chanel.

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:40.449
It was clear that Balsan was willing to sleep
with her, and yet he was ashamed to be seen

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:41.449
with her in public.

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:45.620
Plenty of people would feel completely dejected
by this whole situation.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.250
Instead of feeling defeated, this sparked
a fire in Chanel.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.030
She wanted to prove that she was worthy of
being at this party.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:57.729
The only problem was that the clothes she
arrived in made it obvious that she was poor.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:02.069
So she took one of Balsan’s suits and cut
it apart, tailoring it to fit her body perfectly.

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:04.719
Then, she showed up to the party uninvited.

00:05:04.719 --> 00:05:08.719
She carried herself with confidence, while
everyone’s heads turned to see this beautiful

00:05:08.719 --> 00:05:10.930
woman standing in a man’s suit.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:14.770
When the guests asked why she was dressed
like that, she casually said it was far more

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:15.770
comfortable.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:19.240
Remember- this happened in the year 1906,
so this was completely unheard of.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.220
Women were wearing corsets, long gloves, and
multiple layers of skirts.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.389
At the party, Chanel was clever, and interesting
to talk to.

00:05:26.389 --> 00:05:30.081
When she made new friends, she would make
up elaborate stories about her past, just

00:05:30.081 --> 00:05:31.750
like she did as a young girl.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.189
She once said, “My life didn’t please
me.

00:05:34.189 --> 00:05:36.340
So I created my life.”

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:40.740
Balsan was impressed by this stunt, so he
allowed her to continue living at his Chateau,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.569
and she joined his inner circle of friends.

00:05:42.569 --> 00:05:47.830
He began to treat her to new clothes and jewelry,
but she continued to use the fabric from Balsan’s

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.809
discarded clothing to make herself outfits
to wear, instead.

00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:54.939
For most women, adding layers of fabric, feathers,
and jewels was a way to show off that they

00:05:54.939 --> 00:05:56.830
were married to someone who had a lot of money.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.389
Chanel thought these things were vulgar, and
she didn’t care if a simple style made her

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:02.389
look poor.

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:03.869
She just wanted to be comfortable.

00:06:03.869 --> 00:06:06.939
Soon enough, other women began to copy Coco's
style.

00:06:06.939 --> 00:06:11.069
Looking at photos of Chanel in her youth,
it’s almost as if they were taken today,

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:13.820
or like she was a time traveler sent back
a hundred years.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:19.569
Years later, she was quoted saying, “In
order to be irreplaceable, one must be different.”

00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:23.639
During World War I, women everywhere began
to wear pants, because they had to work while

00:06:23.639 --> 00:06:24.719
their husbands were away.

00:06:24.719 --> 00:06:28.749
But by the time the men returned, they wanted
their wives to go back to wearing dresses.

00:06:28.749 --> 00:06:31.869
Of course, women in the upper class never
had to work at all.

00:06:31.869 --> 00:06:36.240
So they never stopped wearing their corsets
and layers of uncomfortable fabric.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:41.100
If Coco Chanel was going to convince them
to change, it would happen in stages, and

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:46.279
over a very long period of time.

00:06:46.279 --> 00:06:49.809
Love.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:54.029
When she was 26 years old, Gabrielle met an
English businessman named Arthur Capel at

00:06:54.029 --> 00:06:56.409
one of Etienne Balsan’s parties.

00:06:56.409 --> 00:06:59.789
Everyone called him “Boy”, because he
was the illegitimate son of an aristocrat.

00:06:59.789 --> 00:07:02.310
He worked his way up in the world to become
a self-made man.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.430
Out of everyone in Balsan’s inner circle,
he was one of the only people who actually

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:07.999
worked for a living.

00:07:07.999 --> 00:07:12.729
Chanel was not satisfied to sit around and
do nothing all day like other kept women.

00:07:12.729 --> 00:07:17.320
She was earning an income from selling custom-made
hats to women who admired her style, but she

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.419
kept the money in cash.

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:22.899
At the time, women could not own businesses,
rent an apartment, or even have bank accounts

00:07:22.899 --> 00:07:26.389
without a guarantor, which was usually the
father or husband.

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:31.689
Arthur Capel could see that Gabrielle Chanel
was a genius, and he believed in her long

00:07:31.689 --> 00:07:33.020
before anyone else did.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:37.379
He encouraged her to open a shop, and helped
her by putting his name on everything.

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:41.490
Gabrielle ran the business entirely on her
own, and began hiring women to help increase

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.490
production.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:46.009
Boy and Coco were a perfect pair, because
they were both passionate about each of their

00:07:46.009 --> 00:07:48.770
respective businesses, and had mutual respect
for one another.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:53.319
Arthur Capel used his experience to help look
over contracts and negotiate the business

00:07:53.319 --> 00:07:55.589
deals, but the rest was all on her.

00:07:55.589 --> 00:07:59.749
Even before opening her first shop, Chanel
already had loyal clientele from Paris, so

00:07:59.749 --> 00:08:04.879
it became successful right out the gate, and
she began seeing profits almost immediately.

00:08:04.879 --> 00:08:08.819
Boy and Coco used the money to purchase a
lavish townhouse in Paris, which doubled as

00:08:08.819 --> 00:08:09.949
the fashion studio.

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:14.089
The whole of the ground floor was an open
space filled with the workshop.

00:08:14.089 --> 00:08:17.939
She created jobs for women in the local area,
and her staff was growing all the time.

00:08:17.939 --> 00:08:21.999
Upstairs, she kept an apartment, and whenever
Capel was in Paris, he lived there with her.

00:08:21.999 --> 00:08:27.629
But no matter what she did to prove her success,
Coco Chanel could never be seen as the “marrying

00:08:27.629 --> 00:08:29.770
type” in the eyes of the aristocracy.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:34.370
As the member of a noble family, Arthur Capel
was expected to end his affair and marry someone

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:35.470
with a title.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:40.590
In 1918, he wed an English woman named Diana
Wyndham, who was a widow, and related to an

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.660
assortment of Earls and Dukes.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:47.780
But he and Chanel were still very much in
love, and continued their relationship behind

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:48.780
closed doors.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:53.850
On December 22, 1919, Arthur Capel died in
a car crash on his way to spend the holidays

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:54.850
with Coco.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.740
His funeral was on Christmas Eve.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.810
They were together for 9 years, and Chanel
planned to live out the rest of her life with

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.810
him.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.220
She was just 35 years old when he died.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:08.300
Arthur Capel had been the love of her life,
and no other man ever came close to replacing

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.300
him.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.670
Years later, her name would be known around
the world, and those same aristocrats who

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.960
refused to accept her would be fighting to
wear her designs.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:21.090
There came a point in her life when her celebrity
catapulted her to a place where she could

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.840
have married anyone she wanted, but she never
did.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.810
The one man she truly wanted to be her husband
was gone forever.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:32.230
He knew her before, during, and after her
success, and there was no way to replace that.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:36.360
But she had a resilience that helped her to
keep going, no matter what.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.990
She said, “When you’re feeling sad, add
more lipstick, and attack.”

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:40.990
Fashion
After the unexpected death of her beloved

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:41.990
Boy, Coco Chanel needed to find a new business
partner.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:42.990
At that time, she had over 300 employees.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:43.990
She was designing couture dresses that were
selling for over 3,000 francs each.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:11:23.910
In today’s money, that’s more like $38,000
per dress, and she had an entire army of women

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:24.930
making these things.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.710
You would think that this should have proven
that she was more than capable of running

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:29.230
a successful business.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:32.930
But nope- she was still a woman, so the banks
refused to deal with her directly.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:36.590
It would become impossible for her to run
her business on cash alone, and it was completely

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.460
necessary for her to seek help from a male
partner.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:45.940
The law banning women from opening bank accounts
would not change until 1965, after the passing

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.510
of the French Family Law.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.020
This is when she met Pierre Wertheimer.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.960
He had a reputation for working together with
other luxury brands around Paris, and he offered

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.350
to be her business partner.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:12:00.000
The only issue was that Chanel knew nothing
about law or business contracts.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.950
Arthur Capel always had her best interest
at heart, and he gave her the freedom to run

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.620
her business as she pleased, and keep her
profits for herself.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.970
So, she was far too trusting, and unwittingly
signed a contract that said that Pierre Wertheimer

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:15.730
was entitled to take 90% of her business profits.

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:19.610
Even though this contract was ridiculously
unfair, it meant that Chanel could stay in

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.800
business, and she did not let this setback
get the best of her.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:27.320
In 1921, Chanel began working with a celebrity
perfume chemist named Ernest Beaux.

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:31.250
At the time, women were wearing oils that
had a single floral scent.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:34.780
She wanted to create a perfume with a layers
which developed over time.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:39.080
This is when they created Chanel No. 5, and
it became one of the best-selling perfumes

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.240
in the world.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:44.600
For years to come, perfume and candle makers
would copy the idea of mixing various scents

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:47.400
together to create a unique experience.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.470
Before Chanel, women never wore black, unless
they were in mourning.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:55.110
In the 1920’s, Vogue compared her iconic
“little black dress” to Ford’s Model

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:57.580
T. It was simple, elegant, and revolutionary.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.780
Soon enough, people around the world were
looking to Chanel for inspiration.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.730
There was a ripple effect in women’s clothing
in the rest of the world.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:09.410
Without Coco Chanel, there is no telling what
kinds of clothes women would be wearing today.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.480
Years later, Chanel reflected on that time.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:13.390
"I gave women a sense of freedom.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:18.530
I gave them back their bodies: bodies that
were drenched in sweat, due to fashion's finery,

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:21.210
lace, corsets, underclothes, padding."

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:25.280
Despite the fact that she swore off ever marrying,
Chanel continued to be in relationships with

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.280
men.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.760
But no matter how powerful they may have been,
she always stayed true to herself.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:34.500
She dated Grand Duke Dmitri Pavlovich, who
was related to the Russian Romanov family.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.620
Next was Edward VIII, Prince of Wales.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:40.790
And before the dawn of World War II, she began
a relationship with a German man named Baron

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.040
Hans Gunther von Dincklage.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.610
Looking at her track record, it would seem
that she had a personal goal of trying to

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:50.600
see if she could date at least one aristocrat
from each country in Europe.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:55.060
But her decision to be in a relationship with
Von Dincklage would become both a blessing,

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.060
and a curse.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:59.380
Because just a few years later, the Nazi Party
would rise to power, and Chanel’s lover

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:04.250
would reveal his true colors.

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:07.780
War.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:12.720
By the 1930’s, business was absolutely booming,
and they needed all the space they could get

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.960
in the House of Chanel.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:17.590
Her all-female staff increased to 300 workers,
and it became necessary for Chanel to move

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:19.440
out of the studio, and into the Hotel Ritz.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.590
At this point, Chanel had bought up several
stores along a street called The Rue Cambon,

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.090
which ran directly behind The Hotel Ritz.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.380
In 1936, there was a labor movement in France,
and workers were demanding better conditions

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.570
across the country.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:31.990
On April 26th, Coco Chanel arrived at her
studio to see that all 300 of her employees

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:33.770
were sitting on the floor in protest.

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:38.250
They all refused to work, unless their wages
increased and their work hours lessened.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:42.810
Chanel was outraged, because she already paid
these women higher wages and gave more vacation

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:44.710
time than any other business.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:49.570
Instead of giving in to their demands, she
fired all 300 of them on the spot, saying

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:53.140
that they were ingrateful, and she could do
the work on her own.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.450
But they refused to move.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.820
Finally, she gave in to their demands, for
the sake of getting on with the work.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:02.930
In 1939, Germany had occupied Poland, and
Chanel knew it was only a matter of time before

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:03.970
they were coming for France.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:08.040
It’s possible that her boyfriend, Hans Gunther
von Dincklage let her know that the takeover

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.040
was eminent.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:13.480
She laid off all 300 of her workers, and encouraged
them to seek safety before it was too late.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:17.550
Coco Chanel was not going to leave her business,
no matter what happened.

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:19.870
Just three months later, Germany occupied
France.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.910
The Nazis destroyed businesses and homes of
countless number of French people.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:27.880
The Nazis even took over the Hotel Ritz as
their headquarters, so Chanel very literally

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:28.890
had to live among them.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:32.680
Her home and business were both safe, so long
as she continued to be in that relationship

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.680
with Von Dincklage.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:36.050
But, knowing Chanel, she would have hated
this.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:40.250
She never wanted to be beholden to any man,
let alone the ones who thought they could

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.470
rule the world.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:45.060
The Nazis knew that she was close friends
with the British royal family, so they asked

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:48.180
if she would become one of their secret agents
in 1943.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:50.350
She was given the code named “Model Hat”.

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:54.250
On a trip with Von Dincklage, she met with
Winston Churchill, and handed him a letter,

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.830
which gave Germany’s demands for England’s
surrender.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:16:00.270
Obviously, he didn’t take their offer, and
it wouldn’t be surprising if he crumpled

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.839
up the paper where he stood.

00:16:01.839 --> 00:16:05.080
There is no way of knowing what was said between
Churchill and Chanel.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:08.520
Was she actually a double-agent, divulging
Nazi secrets?

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:09.570
We will never know.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:13.410
But when the war was over, Chanel was never
brought to trial for cooperating with the

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.410
Nazis.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:18.380
She never spoke about that time, and buried
it deep, like she did with all of the other

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:20.300
unpleasant memories in her life.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:23.220
Coco Chanel never said anything publicly that
was Anti-Semitic.

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:27.370
The only documented issue she ever had was
with Pierre Wertheimer, who just so happened

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.420
to be Jewish.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.860
After the Nazis occupied France, they were
seizing any property that belonged to the

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.500
Jews, and that included businesses.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:36.610
She wrote a letter to the Nazi government,
asking if there was a chance that she could

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.320
buy back the remaining 90% of House Chanel.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:43.089
However, the family temporarily sold their
business entities to Christians during the

00:16:43.089 --> 00:16:45.339
war, and they had already fled to safety.

00:16:45.339 --> 00:16:50.240
There are plenty of people who cannot forgive
Coco Chanel for cooperating with the Nazis.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:53.980
But for a moment, put yourself in her shoes:
She had two choices.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:57.370
Break up with her boyfriend, condemn the Nazis,
and lose everything.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:02.580
Or, bite her tongue, and keep on pretending,
for the benefit of maintaining the life she

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.050
worked so hard to build.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:05.380
She chose life.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:10.299
And if she were alive today, she probably
wouldn’t even bother to explain her decisions.

00:17:10.299 --> 00:17:12.970
In her own words, “I don’t care what you
think of me.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:15.329
I don’t think about you at all.”

00:17:15.329 --> 00:17:19.220
When the war was over in 1945, Chanel dumped
Von Dinklage quicker than you can say “Auf

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.220
Wiedersehen.”

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:24.230
She moved on to having an affair with the
Spanish artist Salvador Dali, which is an

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:29.379
interesting choice, to say the least.

00:17:29.379 --> 00:17:34.809
Legacy
When the war was over in 1945, Coco Chanel

00:17:34.809 --> 00:17:39.130
was 62 years old, and she no longer felt inspired
to create new clothes.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:42.779
She chose to retire from the fashion world
for years, and lived off of the royalties

00:17:42.779 --> 00:17:44.580
from the sales of her perfume.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.320
In 1958, she found her second wind at the
age of 75.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:51.559
She unveiled new designs, and reopened House
Chanel.

00:17:51.559 --> 00:17:54.009
This sparked a resurgence in her brand’s
popularity.

00:17:54.009 --> 00:17:58.240
Coco Chanel chose a man named Karl Lagerfeld
to be her successor for the brand.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.830
She had more than enough money to retire and
live a comfortable life, but she worked until

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:05.490
the day she died on January 10th, 1971.

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:10.440
When she died, she was 87 years old, and had
an estimated net worth of $100 million.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:14.620
Yes, this sounds like a lot of money, but
keep in mind that Pierre Wertheimer’s grandsons

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:18.369
still own 90% of Chanel, even to this very
day.

00:18:18.369 --> 00:18:20.169
They are now multi-billionaires.

00:18:20.169 --> 00:18:25.100
Today, many people think of Chanel as a brand
that is intimidating and unattainable.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.279
But for those who look at the price tag, they
miss the point.

00:18:28.279 --> 00:18:32.370
Coco Chanel was quoted saying on more than
one occasion that she believed people should

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.450
wear what makes them happy.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:38.649
Wear the colors you feel great in, and the
style that makes you feel comfortable.

00:18:38.649 --> 00:18:43.190
Instead of trying to be flashy or follow a
trend, your attitude and the way you carry

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:46.759
yourself speaks far more than the clothes
on your back.

00:18:46.759 --> 00:18:50.360
She said, “Fashion is not something that
exists in dresses only.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:53.210
Fashion is in the sky, in the street.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:57.350
Fashion has to do with ideas, the way we live,
and what is happening.”

00:18:57.350 --> 00:19:00.350
Now, before we end this video, I just wanted
to say that our audience here on Biographics

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:05.279
is only 13% female, and we look to these analytics
when we decide what videos to make.

00:19:05.279 --> 00:19:09.090
If you’re a woman in the audience, please
do subscribe, so we know you’re out there.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:12.630
And if you felt inspired by the story of Coco
Chanel, please share this with someone in

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:15.289
your life that you know would appreciate it,
too.

00:19:15.289 --> 00:19:17.070
Thanks for watching.

